    dcterms:creator "https://w3id.org/italia/env/ld/common/organisation/ISPRA02" ;
    dcterms:description "Pesticides in groundwater: Contamination levels are determined by comparing measured average concentrations with regulatory limits for surface water and groundwater. The level of the substance is 'over the limits' (level=2) if the concentration is above the EQS, 'within the limits' (level=1) if it's below the EQS and 'non-quantifiable' (level=0) if concentration is below the limit of quantification (LoQ) of the analytical method" ;
